        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Plains of Abraham</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">13 September 1759</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Plains of Abraham, a plateau on the Promontory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> just outside the walls of Quebec City, in the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, now in Quebec, Canada</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> under Major General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-wolfe">James Wolfe</a>, with 4,426 men by the Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>'s figures (from André Charbonneau) or about 7,700 by another count; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Canada under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-joseph-de-montcalm">Marquis de Montcalm</a>, with 2,000 French Army troops, 600 Canadians drafted into regular units and 1,800 militiamen and Indian allies by the same Canadian figures</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French were driven from the field in about an hour. Both generals were mortally wounded, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> capitulated on 18 September.</span></div>
        </div>
